# Compile after code changes

After finishing a change set that touches **compilable** sources, run a compile check before telling the user you are done. Fix failures before finishing.

| Touched paths | Command |
|---|---|
| `app/**/*.kt`, `app/**/*.java`, or Android Gradle under `app/` / root `*.gradle*` | `.\gradlew.bat :app:compileDebugKotlin` (Windows) or `./gradlew :app:compileDebugKotlin` |
| `web/**` (TS/TSX/JS, Next config, etc.) | `npm run build` in `web/` |
| Both Android and web in the same change set | Run both |

## When not to compile

Skip compile when the change set is **only**:

- Markdown / docs under `docs/` or `README*`
- SQL under `supabase/`
- Cursor rules, `.env*` examples, or other non-build assets with no app/web source edits

## Notes

- Prefer the lightest relevant task (`compileDebugKotlin` over full `assembleDebug` unless packaging must be verified).
- If compile fails, fix the code and re-run until it passes (or report a blocker you cannot resolve).
- Do not skip this because the change “looks small.”
